<title>FRANCE: Devaluation talk harmful to EMU -Kohl tells France.</title>
<headline>Devaluation talk harmful to EMU -Kohl tells France.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Talk of softening the criteria for European monetary union or of devaluation within the European Monetary System harms the cause of a single currency, German Chancellor Helmut Kohl said in a French magazine article published on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We (France and Germany) jointly want the euro to be stable. Thus all proposals aiming towards an easing of the criteria or a devaluation within the EMS would be harmful to the common cause,&quot; Kohl wrote in the weekly Le Nouvel Observateur.</p>
<p>He appeared to be responding to ex-president Valery Giscard d'Estaing who has triggered a new debate in France by calling for a weaker franc against the dollar and the euro to revive growth and bring down record unemployment.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
